Cell["\<\
Patterns :
x
x_
x__
x___
x_h
x : pattern
x..
x...
x_ : v
x_.
patt1 | patt2 |...
nameQ[x]
patter ? test
pattern / ; condition
lhs:> rsh /; condiiton
lsh :=rsh /; condition\
\>", "GrayBox"],

Cell["\<\
Transformation rules and difinitions:
exp /. {lhs1->rhs1,...}\t
exp /. rules\ttry rules once
exp //. rules\ttry rules repeatedly until the result no longer changes
lhs = rhs\t(immediate assignment) rhs is evaluated when the assignment is \
made
lhs := rhs\t(delay assignment) rhs is evaluated each time the value of lhs is \
requested
lsh -> rhs\trhs is evaluated when the rule is given
lsh :> rhs\trhs is evaluated when the rule is used
f[x_] := f[x] = rhs\tdefine a funciton which remembers values that it finds
Function[vars,body,{attr}] or body&\t pure function\
\>", "GrayBox"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Mathematica",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " provides a selection of attributes the you can used to specify various \
propreties of functions.\nAttributes[f]\nSetAttributes[f,attr]\nMany \
functions allow you to give additional arguments that specify options\n\
Options[f]\nSetOptions[f,name1->value1,name2->value2,...]\nnames /. options \
/. Options[f]"
}], "GrayBox"],

